{2} - 18y + 64$.$y^{2} - 18y + 64 = ($ {{field-1}} $)^{2} -$\n{{field-2}}"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069186 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068875 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "366b36a5-c909-5ea5-a05d-a6052fcd41d7" :knowledge-point/title "Completing the Square on a Quadratic Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d875ff3-47eb-58c1-b1ae-67c39fc7ba60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532215 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186576406}]}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d875ff3-47eb-58c1-b1ae-67c39fc7ba60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532215} :answer-field/id #uuid "c13619bc-5da4-58c3-8392-a51654138df3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066329} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b3e1513-7c61-5e21-83f2-a7a8ded3d445" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532250 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186576406}]}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b3e1513-7c61-5e21-83f2-a7a8ded3d445" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532250} :answer-field/id #uuid "64193fcd-9f32-5d02-803f-4dc7d03003ea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1b8e89c5-8930-56e1-94ae-d8d80995aed2" :question/math-academy-id "q-250390" :question/problem "If the expression ${x}^{2}+14x+31$ is written as $(x+p)^{2}+q$, then what are the values of $p$ and $q?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,q=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2\\cdot 7x+31\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${7}^{2},$ writing the constant term $31$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}+2\\cdot 7x+{7}^{2}}_{⏟}-\\,{7}^{2}+31\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(x+7)^{2}-{7}^{2}+31\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(x+7)^{2}-18\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=7$ and $q=-18.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069187 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068873 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f10e4a34-a512-5ff4-abbc-66e6830d63d0" :knowledge-point/title "Completing the Square When the Perfect Square is Isolated"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "6917a6cd-a1ab-5653-a227-fcd0d86b22fe" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066331} {:answer-field/id #uuid "79d9c59f-51e6-5163-8f8d-544712045199" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066332}] :question/id #uuid "ca471d39-2701-50bc-b594-f04339afe816" :question/math-academy-id "q-250399" :question/problem "Rewrite the following expression as the difference between a perfect square and a constant.$(x^{2} + 6x + 3^{2}) - 2 = ($ {{field-1}} $)^{2} -$\n{{field-2}}"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069188 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068874 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf9b812d-0dbf-5a67-9d45-3cc5e373b2b1" :knowledge-point/title "Completing the Square When the Perfect Square is Isolated: Negative Linear Term"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "fcdd8b5d-9107-54c8-a658-e9ad470836e1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blan