ally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(y+4{)}^{2}-3.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290595 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068876 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08c6d8d6-3d86-5074-bf99-0cb744c9412a" :knowledge-point/title "Completing the Square on a Quadratic Expression with a Negative Linear Term"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32e0e5d7-fdb8-59c1-ad92-627588672552" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288367}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32e0e5d7-fdb8-59c1-ad92-627588672552" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288367} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4ac6295-516d-5d33-bea7-ff6299cfb972" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290125} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "316891ce-732f-5962-81c6-6104eaf74326" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "316891ce-732f-5962-81c6-6104eaf74326" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288356} :answer-field/id #uuid "f83061da-9749-5727-982b-6f3bd1382a87" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290243}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "14bbb855-11da-520e-8a63-9ebbe8ba5c80" :question/math-academy-id "q-250465" :question/problem "Complete the square on the quadratic expression ${y}^{2}-24y+44.$\n\n${y}^{2}-24y+44=(${{field-1}}${)}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-2\\cdot 12y+44\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${12}^{2},$ writing the constant term $44$ last:\n\n$$\n{{y}^{2}-2\\cdot 12y+{12}^{2}}_{⏟}-\\,{12}^{2}+44\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(y-12{)}^{2}-{12}^{2}+44\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(y-12{)}^{2}-100.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290596 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068876 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08c6d8d6-3d86-5074-bf99-0cb744c9412a" :knowledge-point/title "Completing the Square on a Quadratic Expression with a Negative Linear Term"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b74e78a8-3b6b-549a-b92d-4c311cd6b49b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289246}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b74e78a8-3b6b-549a-b92d-4c311cd6b49b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289246} :answer-field/id #uuid "59cc0709-ad15-565a-99a7-bc43f5f80a0b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289920} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "000ea0dc-e83d-59b3-891d-03ba54bde6ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288025}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "000ea0dc-e83d-59b3-891d-03ba54bde6ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288025} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bd601eb-5637-5c7e-9cf6-b55ee889def4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290036}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 