7x-5\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${7}^{2},$ writing the constant term $-5$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 7x+{7}^{2}}_{⏟}-\\,{7}^{2}-5\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(x-7{)}^{2}-{7}^{2}-5\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(x-7{)}^{2}-54.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=-7$ and $q=-54.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511729 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068876 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08c6d8d6-3d86-5074-bf99-0cb744c9412a" :knowledge-point/title "Completing the Square on a Quadratic Expression with a Negative Linear Term"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d071f54-fccc-5708-b874-70a3ee628a4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-2,\\text{ }q=93" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511720} {:answer/id #uuid "56d5a1e7-ff71-5591-8a56-2626b93dc60d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-2,\\text{ }q=91" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511734} {:answer/id #uuid "69a57b48-df2e-5555-9e1e-824807785fa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=2,\\text{ }q=91" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511738} {:answer/id #uuid "7b98e909-ecee-51dc-8467-4cbed483c0cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-2,\\text{ }q=95" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511745} {:answer/id #uuid "ff66e394-5fe8-5f30-959c-f54117e8978f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-4,\\text{ }q=79" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56d5a1e7-ff71-5591-8a56-2626b93dc60d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-2,\\text{ }q=91" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511734} :answer-field/id #uuid "24591fab-651f-5f9b-bdd0-bb3b130b903f" :answer-field/key "selectio