quare, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(z+12)^{2}-{12}^{2}+153\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(z+12)^{2}+9.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=12$ and $q=9.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511813 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068875 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "366b36a5-c909-5ea5-a05d-a6052fcd41d7" :knowledge-point/title "Completing the Square on a Quadratic Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07f97eb6-3f15-58e0-a328-76cf49f6ab31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=13,\\,q=345" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511773} {:answer/id #uuid "100d06b9-bb76-51b4-bf2f-3fc4172de33a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=13,\\,q=163" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511776} {:answer/id #uuid "2450bea2-611d-577a-959c-3291b52ac5cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=13,\\,q=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511778} {:answer/id #uuid "3f80089c-4bd0-5684-a279-472dcbe3127b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=13,\\,q=176" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511784} {:answer/id #uuid "55087579-8a80-5d26-a160-c59d1fafbec5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=26,\\,q=-500" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2450bea2-611d-577a-959c-3291b52ac5cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=13,\\,q=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511778} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0ca7dcc-bf58-56af-b649-7dc0dca130e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511817}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e5d2f964-7971-5d1d-b830-56c7a04945a9" :question/problem "If the expression ${y}^{2}+26y+176$ is written as $(y+p)^{2}+q$, then what are the values of $p$ and $q$?" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}+2\\cdot 13y+176\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${13}^{2},$ writing the constant term $176$ last:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{{y}^{2}+2\\cdot 13y+{13}^{2}}-\\,{13}^{2}+176\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(y+13)^{2}-{13}^{2}+176\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(y+13)^{2}+7.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=13$ and $q=7.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511815 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068875 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "366b36a5-c909-5ea5-a05d-a6052fcd41d7" :knowledge-point/title "Completing the Square on a Quadratic Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "597e36b5-f1c0-5227-ac21-11afe821395b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=6,\\,q=53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511790} {:answer/id #uuid "7adfd77a-2c35-5839-aba3-20025a57f8bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=6,\\,q=23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511799} {:answer/id #uuid "8f6f60e3-d6aa-5bae-a63d-aad7f1fb4f10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=12,\\,q=-85" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511803} {:answer/id #uuid "94093a8e-c60a-58df-9727-f636c70bb6d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=6,\\,q=59" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511804} {:answer/id #uuid "fe944237-c002-5cd8-adbb-4450570fa880" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=6,\\,q=95" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511821}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7adfd77a-2c35-5839-aba3-20025a57f8bb" :answer/typ