 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}-8x+16)-2 & = \\\\ (x-4)^{2}-2 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532681 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068876 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08c6d8d6-3d86-5074-bf99-0cb744c9412a" :knowledge-point/title "Completing the Square on a Quadratic Expression with a Negative Linear Term"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1932a79d-4e2f-5d3f-a617-e8ffcb8d71aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-6)^{2}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531985} {:answer/id #uuid "5743c63c-942a-5f21-8bac-7ec193c1e106" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-6)^{2}+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532125} {:answer/id #uuid "5e016c46-3617-5f9d-94b5-1c43f2e69e06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-6)^{2}-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532142} {:answer/id #uuid "a4c82222-c3ad-57fc-b6a2-8ef786ebfe1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-12)^{2}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532304} {:answer/id #uuid "f603e514-ee50-5297-9060-98ad3751aeb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-6)^{2}-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e016c46-3617-5f9d-94b5-1c43f2e69e06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-6)^{2}-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532142} :answer-field/id #uuid "4962f429-26e5-56ce-9a63-ab7afa5c8c95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532526}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "93dc778c-0905-5be0-ac96-c8581ce3887e" :question/math-academy-id "q-3661" :question/problem "Complete the square on the quadratic expression ${y}^{2}-12y+15.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-2\\cdot 6y+15\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${6}^{2},$ writing the constant term $15$ last:\n\n$$\n{{y}^{2}-2\\cdot 6y+{6}^{2}}_{⏟}-\\,{6}^{2}+15\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(y-6)^{2}-{6}^{2}+15\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(y-6)^{2}-21.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532698 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068875 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "366b36a5-c909-5ea5-a05d-a6052fcd41d7" :knowledge-point/title "Completing the Square on a Quadratic Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e718716f-1d7d-5c1e-9371-daf7cde9204b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e718716f-1d7d-5c1e-9371-daf7cde9204b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532431} :answer-field/id #uuid "67fff968-5b69-5ebe-bfa8-7177a003e2c4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532539} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f776a6a-8c50-57af-a155-1ddb98fbcde2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f776a6a-8c50-57af-a155-1ddb98fbcde2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532144} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5d7deea-2cab-5d6a-b2d3-2220e5988275" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #e